# An `X "c"` hint names the terminal of the token a parser literal "c"
# would stand for: the lexer rule whose pattern is exactly that text. A
# character class that matches "(" makes no such rule, so the hint names
# no terminal, though OPEN covers "(".
# error: x_hint_class_token.grammar:21:10:
# error: X "(" on expr → IDENT names no token
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    open
    close
    eof
    err
'\n'                                        → skip, skip
[(\[]                                       → open
[)\]]                                       → close
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err
@parser
exprs! = expr+                              → (exprs ...1)
expr   = IDENT X "("                        → (var 1)
       | IDENT OPEN expr CLOSE              → (call 1 3)
       | OPEN expr CLOSE                    → 2
